## Context

Ticket 0469 added `test_main_md_structure.py::test_abstract_numbers_in_body`,
which checks that 0.01 / 0.76 / 0.38 / 0.90 are present somewhere in `main.md`.
This satisfies structural consistency (abstract matches body) but does NOT satisfy
the project's invariant that manuscript numeric literals are re-derived from
committed artifacts (rules/workflow.md: "Derive prose from generated artifacts,
never from agent enumeration").

The body text (§4 Results) itself contains these numbers as hand-authored text
dating to before ticket 0469; no committed macro file exports them.

Investigation during 0469 review revealed an additional issue: the body claims
"16 models × 5 repeats = 80 runs" but `\ExpOneMatrixRuns{70}` (from
`macros_exp1_matrix.tex`) says 70 runs (14 models × 5). The body's "16 models"
references `modelset_ablation_journal` v2 while the matrix was built from
`exp1_batch2` (14 models). The numbers 0.38/0.76/0.01 may also be cohort-
specific. This inconsistency predates ticket 0469 and was not introduced by it.

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — §4 Results paragraph with the hand-authored
  numbers; Abstract repeats them
- `report/inputs/generated/macros_exp1_matrix.tex` — has 70 runs, 14 models
- `src/aedist/tabulate_macros.py` — emits per-model BestModelFOne etc., but
  no cross-run min/max/mean F1 for the Exp1 cohort
- `tests/test_main_md_structure.py` — the current substring-presence test

## Actions

1. Determine the canonical 16-model cohort (or acknowledge the 14 vs 16 discrepancy
   in the body text and correct it to match `\ExpOneMatrixRuns`).
2. Add a new `\ExpOneFOneMin`, `\ExpOneFOneMean`, `\ExpOneFOneMax`, `\ExpOneFOneRho`
   macro set to `tabulate_macros.py` (or a new `tabulate_exp1_run_stats.py`),
   scoped to the canonical Exp1 cohort.
3. Wire the new macro file into `experiments/render.mk`.
4. Update `main.md` §4 Results and Abstract to reference these macros
   (or keep prose but verify the numbers against them in the adherence test).
5. Update `test_main_md_structure.py::test_abstract_numbers_in_body` to re-parse
   the macro file and assert that the manuscript's literals match the macro values.

## Test

The failing-first test is:
```python
def test_abstract_numbers_derived_from_artifact():
    macros = (REPO_ROOT / "report/inputs/generated/macros_exp1_run_stats.tex").read_text()
    # Parse \ExpOneFOneMin{0.01} etc.
    min_f1 = float(re.search(r'\\ExpOneFOneMin\{([^}]+)\}', macros).group(1))
    mean_f1 = float(re.search(r'\\ExpOneFOneMean\{([^}]+)\}', macros).group(1))
    # Abstract must use these exact values (rounded to 2 dp)
    abstract = _abstract_block(_text())
    assert f"{min_f1:.2f}" in abstract
    assert f"{mean_f1:.2f}" in abstract
```

## Verification

- [ ] `macros_exp1_run_stats.tex` is committed and generated by a Makefile rule
- [ ] `test_abstract_numbers_derived_from_artifact` passes
- [ ] Old `test_abstract_numbers_in_body` replaced or upgraded
- [ ] `make -C slides manuscript` still builds
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants

- All other ticket-0469 structural tests continue to pass
- `\ExpOneMatrixRuns` cohort and the run-stats macro cohort must be the same set

## Exit criteria

- At least one abstract numeric literal is re-derived from a committed generated
  artifact, with a failing adherence test if the artifact changes
- The 14 vs 16 model count discrepancy is either corrected or explicitly
  documented as two distinct cohorts (batch2 matrix vs full model set)
